          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong elegant Reedy category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              such that the following
              %em equivalent
              conditions hold
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\hookrightarrow B
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  and every
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in R
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi x
                        %msub
                          %mo ⨿
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi x
                            %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_x \amalg_{L_x A} L_x B \to B_x
                  is a monomorphism.
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
                  of codegeneracy maps in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                  has an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+colimit"} absolute
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mo −
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
              %li
                %p
                  Every element of a presheaf
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  is a degeneracy of some nondegenerate element in a unique way.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The principal theorem about elegant Reedy categories is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            (i.e. contravariant diagrams) over an elegant Reedy category coincides with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+model+structure"} injective model structure
            %em any
            model category, only well-behaved ones. We clarify the necessary conditions by building up to this theorem in stages, adding hypotheses on the codomain of the presheaves as necessary.
          %h3#degeneracies_are_split Degeneracies are split
          #DegSplit.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is elegant, then every codegeneracy map (i.e. morphism in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} split epimorphism
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:x\to y
              be a codegeneracy map; then the span
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi f
                    %mi x
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \xleftarrow{f} x \xrightarrow{f} y
              has an absolute pushout, consisting of say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:y\to z
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:y\to z
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi h
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f = h f
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(z,-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_z\in R(z,z)
              must be the image under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              of some map
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi z
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:z\to y
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_z = g s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s h:y\to y
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_y
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi s
                      %mi h
                      %mo =
                      %mi h
                      %mo =
                      %mi h
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g s h = h = h 1_y
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(y,-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(y,z)
              relating
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s h
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t:y\to x
              such that
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f t = 1_y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is split epi.
          #MonoPreservesDeg.num_lemma
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For every monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\hookrightarrow B
              of presheaves on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              remains nondegenerate in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              be a nondegenerate element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
              a codegeneracy map, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B_y
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi f
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_f b = a
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \id
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegSplit"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              has a section
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s: y \to x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi s
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi f
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_s a = B_s B_f b = b
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in A_y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is nondegenerate, it follows that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \id
          %h3#degeneracies_in_subobjects Degeneracies in subobjects
          #DegSub.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be elegant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:x\to y
              a codegeneracy in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be any category, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu:A\to B
              a monomorphism in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi R
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{R^{\mathrm{op}}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi A
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ A_y &amp; \xrightarrow{A_f} &amp; A_x \\
                    {}^{\mu_y}\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^{\mu_x} \\
                    B_y &amp; \xrightarrow{B_f} &amp; B_x  }
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This depends only on the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is split epi in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:y\to x
              be a section of it, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be the pullback of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_f
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:P\to A_x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
